{{!--
  Give Feedback (issue #8893): what a person wrote to the team that reads
  it - the OneUptime team on OneUptime Cloud, a self-hosted server's admins
  at its Admin Notification Email - sent by the server
  (Common/Server/Utils/ProductFeedback/GiveFeedbackEmail.ts). The person is
  copied on it (Cc) and a reply goes to them (Reply-To), so the same email
  reads right in both inboxes.

  Every value below but this file's own words is the person's or their
  project's: each row is plainText, which Handlebars escapes. messageHtml is
  what they wrote with its line breaks kept: GiveFeedbackEmail
  (getGiveFeedbackMessageHtml) escapes every line and adds nothing but the
  <br/> between them. preheader - what it is about, who wrote and their
  project, for the inbox's preview line - is read by the Start partial
  above, which escapes it.
--}}

{{> InfoBlock plainInfo="Sent with Give Feedback. The person who wrote it is copied on this email, and a reply goes to them."}}

{{> DetailBoxStart this }}
{{> DetailBoxField title="What it is about" plainText=category }}
{{> DetailBoxField title="What they wrote" blockText=messageHtml }}
{{> DetailBoxField title="Name" plainText=personName }}
{{> DetailBoxField title="Email" plainText=personEmail }}
{{> DetailBoxField title="Project" plainText=projectName }}
{{> DetailBoxField title="Project ID" plainText=projectId }}
{{> DetailBoxField title="Page" plainText=page }}
{{> DetailBoxField title="Version" plainText=version }}
{{> DetailBoxEnd this }}

